    "result_text": "The full suite is just the acceptance test (2 tests), and it passes. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `ownerSegment` following the repo's established one-policy-per-derived-field pattern, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerSegmentPolicy.java`** (a small, self-contained unit with no surrounding class complexity):\n- `ownerSegment(owner)` composes `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n  - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`, reusing `OwnerMembershipCeilingPolicy.cappedMembershipLevel` (the same value exposed as the DTO's `membershipLevel`).\n  - AREA = `METRO` when the locality is in `{NSW, VIC, QLD}` else `REGIONAL`, reusing `OwnerLocalityPolicy.locality`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line wiring `ownerSegment` to the new policy (the mapper is a MapStruct interface, so CC is effectively 1 and I only added a single annotation line).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nI deliberately avoided touching or growing any existing complex method \u2014 the derivation lives entirely in a fresh, trivial class and is composed from two existing policies rather than reimplementing their logic. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
